Second ascension ever :) The first one was helped massively by advice
from the lovely folks in #nethack on freenode. This one I did mostly on
my own (with a little advice on the wishes). I wasn't as lucky as in my
first asc, so I'm considering this one to be my first ascension based
on skill not luck.

First thing of interest was getting Cleaver from sacrifice. This ended
up being my weapon for the entire game. Was lucky enough to find a bag
of holding in a shop, solving the space problem. Sokoban gave me an
Amulet of Reflection, so I was quite well set... and even more so when
I found a wizard's bones near the bottom of the Mines, giving me a
Cloak of Magic Resistance and cheering me up a lot :)

Descent through the dungeon was unremarkable, except for the number of
small thronerooms - three of them, none larger than 3x3. Didn't get
anything from them though, they vanished quickly. The drawbridge was
quickly destroyed (not by me) when I got to the Castle, irritating as
I'd planned to squish everything with it. Fought everything inside the
hard way, and got the wishes. I'd already gotten two artifacts from
sacrifice, annoyingly, and a third was generated inside the castle, so
wishing for artifacts was out. Fortunately I had a scroll of charging
already, so I was able to use all six wishes on things I needed. SDSM,
boots of speed, 2 blessed genocide scrolls, magic marker and ring of
conflict. Promptly wiped out h and L, went back up to do the Quest and
Ludios (for the last bit of protection, as well as throne, I was
getting annoyed with nothing happening at all, at any throne). Another
couple of artifacts were gifted to me, during my sacrifices at the
time.

Gehennom was quite straightforward thanks to the magic mapping provided
by my magic marker, and I wrested the last wish out to give me another
magic marker when it ran out. Only fought Orcus, the first two princes
were bribed and for some reason Juiblex wasn't there. The Wizard was
quite straightforward, he fell to the first blast of Death, and I was
able to nip down and grab the amulet. The ascent was slow, due to the
annoying number of teleport that occured when I tried to climb, but I
got all the way out, only having to kill the wizard once en route.
Thanks to Conflict, the elemental planes were straightforward too,
though there were a couple of nasty moments with air elementals. Had to
visit all three altars, but conflict and teleport wands helped make it
possible. And ascended with far more artifacts in my bag than is good
for me - one from the castle, one from a bones pile and too many from
my god, Set.

Quite proud :) My second ascension,but not nearly as lucky as my first
(I had eight wishes in that one, one of them on Dlevel 2). And I did it
with three conducts intact - both polys and artiwishless.

w00t. I can be awarded the Birdie trophy now in the tournament :) It
should be nice, I'm the one that did the art for it after all ;)

Calamarain, chaotic male orcish Barbarian




